---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { planets } from "../../data/planets";
---
<SiteLayout title="Interactive Solar System tools" description="Explore ORRERYA's free planetary calculators, orbital mechanics lab, JPL-based planet position explorer and planetary correlation tools.">
  <div class="container breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Interactive tools</span></div>
  <header class="page-intro container"><div class="eyebrow">SOLAR SYSTEM TOOLS</div><h1>Solar System calculators<br />and interactive models.</h1><p class="lede">Change a value, choose another world or convert a distance. Each tool shows the calculation behind its result.</p></header>
  <section class="section container">
    <div class="calculator-launch-grid" aria-label="Quick calculators">
      <button class="calculator-launch-card" type="button" data-open-tool="weight" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="weight"><span class="eyebrow">Tool 01 · Gravity</span><strong>How much would you weigh on other worlds?</strong><span class="text-link">Open calculator ↗</span></button>
      <button class="calculator-launch-card" type="button" data-open-tool="distance" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="distance"><span class="eyebrow">Tool 02 · Distance & light</span><strong>How far is an AU?</strong><span class="text-link">Open calculator ↗</span></button>
      <button class="calculator-launch-card" type="button" data-open-tool="compare" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="compare"><span class="eyebrow">Tool 03 · Planetary scale</span><strong>Compare planet sizes.</strong><span class="text-link">Open calculator ↗</span></button>
      <button class="calculator-launch-card" type="button" data-open-tool="year" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="year"><span class="eyebrow">Tool 04 · Orbital period</span><strong>How long is a year?</strong><span class="text-link">Open calculator ↗</span></button>
    </div>
    <dialog class="tool-dialog" id="weight" aria-labelledby="weight-title"><article class="card tool-panel tool-dialog-panel">
        <div class="tool-dialog-top"><span class="eyebrow">Tool 01 · Gravity</span><button type="button" class="tool-dialog-close" data-close-tool aria-label="Close calculator">×</button></div><h2 id="weight-title">How much would you weigh on other worlds?</h2><p>Mass is the amount of matter in you. Weight is the gravitational force acting on that mass. Your mass stays the same as you travel; your weight changes with local gravity.</p>
        <div class="field"><label for="mass-input">Your mass (kilograms)</label><input id="mass-input" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" step="any" value="70" inputmode="decimal" /></div>
        <div class="field"><label for="gravity-world">Choose a world</label><select id="gravity-world">{planets.map((planet)=><option value={planet.gravityValue} data-name={planet.name} selected={planet.slug === "earth"}>{planet.name}</option>)}</select></div>
        <div class="result-box" aria-live="polite"><span>Gravitational force on you</span><strong id="weight-result">686 N</strong><span id="weight-subresult">Equivalent to about 70 kg on an Earth-calibrated scale.</span></div>
        <p class="tool-footnote">Model: W = m × g. Uses JPL's equatorial gravitational acceleration (GM/r²); it does not subtract centrifugal acceleration from rotation. A real scale reading is effective gravity and varies with latitude, altitude, rotation and local mass distribution. For giant planets, the equatorial reference is the 1-bar level. This is a gravity-only teaching estimate, not a prediction of how a spacesuit or spacecraft behaves.</p>
      </article></dialog>
    <dialog class="tool-dialog" id="distance" aria-labelledby="distance-title"><article class="card tool-panel tool-dialog-panel">
        <div class="tool-dialog-top"><span class="eyebrow">Tool 02 · Distance & light</span><button type="button" class="tool-dialog-close" data-close-tool aria-label="Close calculator">×</button></div><h2 id="distance-title">How far is an AU?</h2><p>An astronomical unit (AU) is defined as exactly 149,597,870.7 kilometres. It is a useful unit for measuring distances within planetary systems.</p>
        <div class="field"><label for="au-input">Distance (AU)</label><input id="au-input" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" step="any" value="1" inputmode="decimal" /></div>
        <div class="result-box" aria-live="polite"><span>Distance in kilometres</span><strong id="km-result">149,597,871 km</strong><span id="light-result">Light travel time: 8 min 19 s</span></div>
        <p class="tool-footnote">Uses the exact AU definition and the speed of light in vacuum, 299,792.458 km/s. Light time is a simple straight-line vacuum calculation.</p>
      </article></dialog>
    <dialog class="tool-dialog" id="compare" aria-labelledby="compare-title"><article class="card tool-panel tool-dialog-panel">
        <div class="tool-dialog-top"><span class="eyebrow">Tool 03 · Planetary scale</span><button type="button" class="tool-dialog-close" data-close-tool aria-label="Close calculator">×</button></div><h2 id="compare-title">Compare planet sizes.</h2><p>Compare a planet's equatorial diameter with Earth's. The circles use a common scale, capped so the largest planet fits on the card.</p>
        <div class="field"><label for="size-world">Choose a planet</label><select id="size-world">{planets.map((planet)=><option value={planet.diameterKm} data-name={planet.name} data-mass={planet.mass1024} selected={planet.slug === "earth"}>{planet.name}</option>)}</select></div>
        <div class="size-stage"><div id="size-orb" class="size-orb" style="width:56px;height:56px"></div><div><strong id="size-name">Earth</strong><span id="size-diameter">12,756 km diameter</span><b id="size-ratio">1.00 × Earth's diameter</b><small id="mass-ratio">1.00 × Earth's mass</small></div></div>
        <div class="scale-legend"><span>Relative diameter</span><span>Earth = 1</span></div>
        <div class="scale-track"><span id="scale-fill" style="width:8.9%"></span></div>
        <p class="tool-footnote">The circle represents diameter only. The labels compare diameter and mass with Earth; the circle does not encode mass, density or surface area. Planet images are not drawn to this scale.</p>
      </article></dialog>
    <dialog class="tool-dialog" id="year" aria-labelledby="year-title"><article class="card tool-panel tool-dialog-panel">
        <div class="tool-dialog-top"><span class="eyebrow">Tool 04 · Orbital period</span><button type="button" class="tool-dialog-close" data-close-tool aria-label="Close calculator">×</button></div><h2 id="year-title">How long is a year?</h2><p>A planet's orbital period is the time it takes to complete one orbit around the Sun relative to distant stars.</p>
        <div class="field"><label for="year-world">Choose a planet</label><select id="year-world">{planets.map((planet)=><option value={planet.orbitDays} data-name={planet.name} selected={planet.slug === "earth"}>{planet.name}</option>)}</select></div>
        <div class="result-box" aria-live="polite"><span>One sidereal orbit</span><strong id="year-result">365.2 days</strong><span id="year-subresult">About 1.00 Earth years.</span></div>
        <p class="tool-footnote">Uses NASA/JPL sidereal orbital periods, converted from Julian years using 365.25 days per Julian year. The Earth-year comparison uses Earth's JPL sidereal orbital period. A sidereal orbital period is measured relative to distant stars; it is not a planet's solar day or a seasonal year.</p>
      </article></dialog>
    <div class="lab-launch-grid" aria-label="Advanced planetary labs">
      <a class="lab-launch-card" href="/tools/ephemeris/">
        <span class="eyebrow">Tool 06 · JPL approximate ephemeris</span><h2>Planet position explorer</h2>
        <p>Choose a date and see the eight planets projected around the Sun, with geometric distances and EMB-relative directions. The Earth row is a barycentre proxy, not a lunar-resolved geocentre.</p><span class="text-link">Explore planetary positions ↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="lab-launch-card" href="/tools/correlation-lab/">
        <span class="eyebrow">Tool 07 · Planetary data</span><h2>Planetary correlation lab</h2>
        <p>Choose any two of seven physical or orbital properties, switch between linear and logarithmic axes, and inspect the relationship.</p><span class="text-link">Explore planetary data ↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <a class="lab-launch-card orbit-model-launch" href="/tools/orbit-model/"><span class="eyebrow">Tool 05 · Orbital mechanics</span><h2>Move a planet around its orbit.</h2><p>Choose a planet and move it through its orbit. Watch its distance from the Sun and orbital speed change between perihelion and aphelion.</p><span class="text-link">Open orbital mechanics model ↗</span></a>
    <div class="callout tools-note"><strong>These are transparent educational models.</strong><p>They use rounded reference values and standard equations. They are not a navigation system, a live ephemeris or a precision engineering tool. Open the linked NASA/JPL references for definitions, uncertainties and higher-precision parameters.</p></div>
    <div class="source-panel"><div><span class="eyebrow">Calculation references</span><h3>Sources and constants</h3><p>Planetary gravity and orbital values are taken from NASA/JPL and NASA NSSDCA tables.</p></div><ul class="source-list"><li><a href="https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/planets/phys_par.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">NASA/JPL — Planetary Physical Parameters ↗</a></li><li><a href="https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/planetary/factsheet/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">NASA NSSDCA — Planetary Fact Sheet ↗</a></li><li><a href="https://www.iau.org/public/themes/measuring/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">International Astronomical Union — Measuring the Universe ↗</a></li></ul></div>
  </section>
  <script>
    import {
      ASTRONOMICAL_UNIT_KM,
      SPEED_OF_LIGHT_KM_S,
      EARTH_SIDEREAL_YEAR_DAYS
    } from "../../lib/scientific-constants.js";
    const formatter = new Intl.NumberFormat("en-US", { maximumFractionDigits: 2 });
    const massInput = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("#mass-input");
    const gravitySelect = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("#gravity-world");
    const weightResult = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#weight-result");
    const weightSub = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#weight-subresult");
    function updateWeight() {
      if (!massInput || !gravitySelect || !weightResult || !weightSub) return;
      const mass = Number(massInput.value);
      const gravity = Number(gravitySelect.value);
      if (!Number.isFinite(mass) || mass < 0 || !Number.isFinite(gravity)) {
        weightResult.textContent = "Enter a valid mass";
        weightSub.textContent = "Use a non-negative number in kilograms.";
        return;
      }
      const force = mass * gravity;
      weightResult.textContent = formatter.format(force) + " N";
      weightSub.textContent = "About " + formatter.format(force / 9.80665) + " kg-force on an Earth-calibrated scale · " + (gravitySelect.selectedOptions[0]?.dataset.name || "selected world");
    }
    massInput?.addEventListener("input", updateWeight);
    gravitySelect?.addEventListener("change", updateWeight);
    update  <script>

    import {
      ASTRONOMICAL_UNIT_KM,
      SPEED_OF_LIGHT_KM_S,
      EARTH_SIDEREAL_YEAR_DAYS
    } from "../../lib/scientific-constants.js";
    const formatter = new Intl.NumberFormat("en-US", { maximumFractionDigits: 2 });
    function pulseResult(target: HTMLElement | null) {
      if (!target) return;
      target.classList.remove("result-updated");
      void target.offsetWidth;
      target.classList.add("result-updated");
    }
    const massInput = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("#mass-input");
    const gravitySelect = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("#gravity-world");
    const weightResult = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#weight-result");
    const weightSub = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#weight-subresult");
    const weightBox = weightResult?.closest(".result-box") as HTMLElement | null;
    function updateWeight(animate = false) {
      if (!massInput || !gravitySelect || !weightResult || !weightSub) return;
      const mass = Number(massInput.value);
      const gravity = Number(gravitySelect.value);
      if (!Number.isFinite(mass) || mass < 0 || !Number.isFinite(gravity)) {
        weightResult.textContent = "Enter a valid mass";
        weightSub.textContent = "Use a non-negative number in kilograms.";
        return;
      }
      const force = mass * gravity;
      weightResult.textContent = formatter.format(force) + " N";
      weightSub.textContent = "About " + formatter.format(force / 9.80665) + " kg-force on an Earth-calibrated scale · " + (gravitySelect.selectedOptions[0]?.dataset.name || "selected world");
      if (animate) pulseResult(weightBox);
    }
    massInput?.addEventListener("input", () => updateWeight(true));
    gravitySelect?.addEventListener("change", () => updateWeight(true));
    updateWeight();

    const auInput = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("#au-input");
    const kmResult = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#km-result");
    const lightResult = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#light-result");
    const distanceBox = kmResult?.closest(".result-box") as HTMLElement | null;
    function updateDistance(animate = false) {
      if (!auInput || !kmResult || !lightResult) return;
      const au = Number(auInput.value);
      if (!Number.isFinite(au) || au < 0) {
        kmResult.textContent = "Enter a valid distance";
        lightResult.textContent = "Use a non-negative number of AU.";
        return;
      }
      const km = au * ASTRONOMICAL_UNIT_KM;
      const seconds = km / SPEED_OF_LIGHT_KM_S;
      const hours = Math.floor(seconds / 3600);
      const minutes = Math.floor((seconds % 3600) / 60);
      const remain = Math.round(seconds % 60);
      kmResult.textContent = formatter.format(km) + " km";
      lightResult.textContent = hours > 0 ? "Light travel time: " + hours + " h " + minutes + " min " + remain + " s" : "Light travel time: " + minutes + " min " + remain + " s";
      if (animate) pulseResult(distanceBox);
    }
    auInput?.addEventListener("input", () => updateDistance(true));
    updateDistance();

    const sizeSelect = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("#size-world");
    const sizeOrb = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#size-orb");
    const sizeName = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#size-name");
    const sizeDiameter = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#size-diameter");
    const sizeRatio = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#size-ratio");
    const massRatio = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#mass-ratio");
    const scaleFill = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#scale-fill");
    const sizeStage = sizeOrb?.closest(".size-stage") as HTMLElement | null;
    function updateSize(animate = false) {
      if (!sizeSelect || !sizeOrb || !sizeName || !sizeDiameter || !sizeRatio || !massRatio || !scaleFill) return;
      const diameter = Number(sizeSelect.value);
      const mass = Number(sizeSelect.selectedOptions[0]?.dataset.mass);
      const ratio = diameter / 12756;
      const massMultiple = mass / 5.97217;
      const visualSize = Math.max(13, Math.min(188, 56 * ratio));
      sizeOrb.style.width = visualSize + "px";
      sizeOrb.style.height = visualSize + "px";
      sizeName.textContent = sizeSelect.selectedOptions[0]?.dataset.name || "Selected world";
      sizeDiameter.textContent = formatter.format(diameter) + " km diameter";
      sizeRatio.textContent = formatter.format(ratio) + " × Earth's diameter";
      massRatio.textContent = formatter.format(massMultiple) + " × Earth's mass";
      scaleFill.style.width = Math.min(100, (diameter / 142984) * 100) + "%";
      if (animate) pulseResult(sizeStage);
    }
    sizeSelect?.addEventListener("change", () => updateSize(true));
    updateSize();

    const yearSelect = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("#year-world");
    const yearResult = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#year-result");
    const yearSub = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#year-subresult");
    const yearBox = yearResult?.closest(".result-box") as HTMLElement | null;
    function updateYear(animate = false) {
      if (!yearSelect || !yearResult || !yearSub) return;
      const days = Number(yearSelect.value);
      yearResult.textContent = formatter.format(days) + " days";
      yearSub.textContent = "About " + formatter.format(days / EARTH_SIDEREAL_YEAR_DAYS) + " Earth years · " + (yearSelect.selectedOptions[0]?.dataset.name || "selected world");
      if (animate) pulseResult(yearBox);
    }
    yearSelect?.addEventListener("change", () => updateYear(true));
    updateYear();
    const calculatorDialogs = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLDialogElement>(".tool-dialog"));
    function openCalculator(id: string, addHistory = true) {
      const dialog = calculatorDialogs.find((item) => item.id === id);
      if (!dialog) return;
      if (!dialog.open) dialog.showModal();
      if (addHistory && location.hash !== "#" + id) {
        history.pushState({ ...(history.state || {}), orreryaCalculator: id }, "", location.pathname + location.search + "#" + id);
      }
      const focusTarget = dialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>('input:not([type="hidden"]), select, button');
      if (focusTarget) requestAnimationFrame(() => focusTarget.focus({ preventScroll: true }));
    }
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-open-tool]").forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener("click", () => openCalculator(button.dataset.openTool || ""));
    });
    calculatorDialogs.forEach((dialog) => {
      dialog.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-close-tool]")?.addEventListener("click", () => dialog.close());
      dialog.addEventListener("click", (event) => { if (event.target === dialog) dialog.close(); });
      dialog.addEventListener("close", () => {
        if (location.hash === "#" + dialog.id) {
          if (history.state?.orreryaCalculator === dialog.id) history.back();
          else history.replaceState(history.state, "", location.pathname + location.search);
        }
      });
    });
    function syncCalculatorFromUrl() {
      const id = decodeURIComponent(location.hash.slice(1));
      calculatorDialogs.forEach((dialog) => { if (dialog.id !== id && dialog.open) dialog.close(); });
      if (id && calculatorDialogs.some((dialog) => dialog.id === id)) openCalculator(id, false);
    }
    window.addEventListener("popstate", syncCalculatorFromUrl);
    syncCalculatorFromUrl();

  </script>;padding:27px;scroll-margin-top:100px}.orbit-lab-heading{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-start;gap:25px;margin-bottom:20px}.orbit-lab-heading h2{font-size:1.9rem;margin:8px 0}.orbit-lab-heading p{max-width:690px;font-size:.86rem;line-height:1.75;margin:0}.orbit-lab-layout{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr .9fr;gap:22px}.orbit-canvas{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:7px;background:radial-gradient(ellipse at 40% 50%,rgba(45,79,119,.2),transparent 62%),#091321;padding:12px;min-width:0}.orbit-canvas svg{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}.orbit-legend{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:15px;color:var(--quiet);font-size:.68rem;padding:5px 8px}.orbit-legend span{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px}.orbit-legend i{width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;display:inline-block}.legend-sun{background:#edb966;box-shadow:0 0 9px #edb96688}.legend-planet{background:#8bc9dc}.orbit-controls{display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center}.orbit-controls .field{margin-top:11px}.orbit-controls input[type=range]{accent-color:var(--gold);padding:0;min-height:30px}.orbit-play-row{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-top:12px;flex-wrap:wrap}.orbit-play-row .btn{min-height:44px}.orbit-play-status{flex:1;min-width:180px;color:var(--quiet);font-size:.72rem;line-height:1.5;margin:0}.orbit-controls output{float:right;color:var(--gold);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.orbit-result-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:10px;margin-top:18px}.orbit-result{padding:14px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:5px;background:rgba(9,18,31,.7)}.orbit-result span,.orbit-result small{display:block;color:var(--quiet);font-size:.67rem}.orbit-result strong{display:block;color:var(--gold-bright);font:600 1.25rem "Space Grotesk",sans-serif;margin:7px 0 3px}.orbit-endpoints{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:10px;margin-top:10px}.orbit-endpoints div{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:10px}.orbit-endpoints span{display:block;color:var(--quiet);font-size:.67rem}.orbit-endpoints strong{display:block;color:var(--text);font-size:.85rem;margin-top:3px}.orbit-model-note{font-size:.69rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--quiet);margin:16px 0 0}.orbit-equations{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;margin-top:18px;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.orbit-equations>div{display:grid;gap:8px}.orbit-equations strong{font:500 clamp(.92rem,2vw,1.18rem) "Space Grotesk",sans-serif;color:var(--cyan)}.lab-launch-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:15px;margin:30px 0}.lab-launch-card{display:block;padding:24px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:7px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#142238,#0b1423);transition:transform .2s,border-color .2s}.lab-launch-card:hover{transform:translateY(-3px);border-color:rgba(230,200,142,.48)}.lab-launch-card h2{font-size:1.45rem;margin:10px 0}.lab-launch-card p{font-size:.82rem;line-height:1.7;min-height:56px}.lab-launch-card .text-link{font-size:.76rem}.tools-note{margin-top:28px}.source-panel{margin-top:35px}@media(max-width:850px){.orbit-lab-layout{grid-template-columns:1fr}}@media(max-width:760px){.lab-launch-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.tools-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.tool-panel>p{min-height:0}.orbit-lab{padding:19px}.orbit-lab-heading{flex-direction:column}.orbit-equations{grid-template-columns:1fr}.orbit-result-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}@media(max-width:470px){.tool-panel{padding:19px}.size-stage{gap:12px;padding:12px}.size-stage strong{font-size:1rem}}
  </style>
</SiteLayout>
